ent  the digital pcr approach was used to  determine the gene editing efficiencies  the results vary depending on the single  guide rna used  the gene editing efficiency for the  track locus was 45  the gene editing efficiency for the trb  locus was 15  and the gene editing efficiency for the  pd1 locus  was 20 percent at the asgct meeting this  year  dr carl dune affirmed that the reagents  used for gene editing have come a long  way from the first generation reagents  that were used in this study they are  now getting  over 90 gene editing efficiencies for  the three loci  as they embark on expanding this trial  to include a larger cohort of patients  the high fidelity on target editing for  track  and pd-1 was well over 99  it was a little lower for the trb locus  but then the gene editing efficiency was  lower for this locus as well  when the nice cells were co-cultured  with the target cells expressing the new  york eso one tumor antigen  in an in vitro cytotoxicity assay  the nice cells demonstrated potent  antigen-specific cytotoxicity  over a wide range of effector to target  ratios  in fact the nice cells showed even  greater cytotoxicity  than the control cells that expressed  the transgenic tcr  but were electroporated without the  crisper reagents  in another assay to assess the  polyfunctional profile  the nice cells that were activated with  the cd3cd28 beads  secreted very high levels of interferon  gamma  in response to the target cell  the patient outcomes after the infusion  of nice cells  were encouraging the frequencies of the  gene edited  in tcr engineered cells remained quite  stable  between day 10 and 4 months post  infusion  there was also an increase in the  expression of genes  associated with the central memory  phenotype  these data are not shown here  samples were collected from patients  between three  and nine months post infusion and  expanded in the presence of new york eso  one antigen  antigen-specific cytotoxicity was  assessed  by chromium release assays and was  observed  in all patients the ct scan from one  patient  also showed a 50 regression  of a large abdominal mass  these case studies illustrate the  diverse applications  of maxsites technology in the car tcr  field the non-viral approach  discussed here is robust safe  and cost-effective the mrna car  therapies in resting and activated  t-cells  and also in nk cells are efficacious  with no serious side effects  it is possible to generate potent  piggyback transposon  cars that can be translated rapidly  to the clinic gene editing can not only  be used to generate  allogeneic cell therapy products but  also to improve the efficacy  of an already existing cell therapy  product  at macsite we have a partnership  approach to our science  we have a globally distributed  goal-oriented  field applications and sales team  we have a very experienced in-house r d  team we also have a skilled  quality and regulatory affairs team who  handle  our fda master file and quality  documentation  macsite's expert platform is more than  just a technology  it is a solution  thank you for listening and for your  patience  i can now take your questions  all right thank you rama so much for  your informative presentation  i'd like to use the remaining portion of  the session to now ask rama any  questions our viewers might have  so if you have a question you'd like to  ask please just do so now by using the  ask a question box located at the far  left of your screen  all right let's get started so rama  does maxsight have experience with other  transposon technologies  and if so what is the technology and  what is the performance  related to the technology  uh hi leslie can you hear me can  everybody hear me  yes rama okay great so  yes the answer is yes maxsite is working  with  a lot of companies with their  proprietary  transfers on technologies and also with  other pi specifically working with  sleeping beauty based uh car products  and other  piggyback transposons or piggy bat  transposon technologies so this  technology is used in both activated t  cells as well as  in cd4 and cd8 positive t  cells we have seen from our data from  the customers that we do get superior  transfection efficiencies when compared  to  lentiviral transduction of transposons  so i would say like we have efficiencies  that are consistent  and reproducible and some of the groups  have reported  well over 70 percent efficiency in  transfecting transposons okay  next question how does mrna-based gene  delivery systems  work when it's transient it may not give  a sustained  efficacy against tumor or relapse so  what is the argument behind this  approach  that's a really good question uh because  i presented so many case studies  on mrna transfection so  so the argument is you would think of an  mrna  car approach is more like a hit and run  approach like you would see with  bi-specific  antibodies and other  you know antibody therapies but  specifically  how the advantages of doing the mrna  therapy  is you will have to do repeated  infusions of the mrna car product as we  saw  in our case studies and the advantage of  that  is as you know car therapies and tcr  therapies to a lesser extent but car  therapies typically have a lot of  serious side effects and cytokine  release syndrome  and such that are evident when  the in the prolonged expression of car  gave given using viral vector  methodology so mrna  therapies can control that so since they  are given as  repeated injections one can actually  stop the injection  when the patients succumb to  some kind of cytokine release syndrome  and as evidenced in some of our case  studies  we have seen pretty efficacious  and robust response that is very target  specific and not  of tumor of tumor toxicities as seen in  the first clinical trial  with epitope spreading so that was  really successful  okay great um rama you had mentioned  the cryo preservation as part of the  workflow during t