e the last question unless we get  any more after this one but  are there any clinical trials or  products in the market using  uh your non-viral approach  yes so as i showed in the  um in in the talk uh  we ourselves are engaged in a in a  clinically  max site ourselves engaged in a karma  clinical trial that's ongoing  and we do have a number of customers  that are using  our technology in in a variety of ways  in the clinic  whether it's in transposon therapies  they're either well  on their way into getting into a clinic  they're  working on their pre-ind filing or  they're  in their non-human primate studies and  will  very soon get into clinical trials or  um with we are also as i mentioned in  the last case study  a number of our customers are using us  in  allogeneic approaches uh that are  already in clinic right now so we  are upstream of the car process or  downstream where we  uh used to delete the the  track b2m to create an allotment product  so the answer is yes and there are other  other car therapies  that are non-viral therapies that are  also  well on their way to being in the clinic  or already in the clinic  okay great so it doesn't look like we  have any more  questions coming in so um with that i'll  go ahead and actually wrap up the  session um so i wanted to remind  all of our audience members that the  recorded version of today's talk  will be made available soon after this  live session  so you will be notified via email when  it becomes available  on also any questions that were unable  to be answered today  via the actual live session the answers  will be provided to you  in the in in using the email address you  provided at the time of registration  as well any that come through during the  on-demand period  so before we go i do want to take some  time to thank rama for her very detailed  presentation  a thank you to the customers industry  partners for allowing us to share your  important work with the larger cell and  gene therapy community  and i also want to thank lab roots and  their supportive webinar team  for organizing and promoting our event  lastly i would like to thank you  our audience participants for joining us  today and for your interesting questions  we look forward to having you in  attendance at our next midnight  lab roots sponsored session on september  17th  featuring our scalable manufacturing and  nano vesicle delivering solution using  crispr cas9 rmps  so this will conclude our session for  today until next time  goodbye bye
 

